{"assets":["/statement-assets/2cf57a7cc68ee97e58b245c382570db74b333cf767ab88a556bab8496c6d31f0.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"703","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Chris and Road"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And while Mishka is enjoying her trip..."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Chris is a little brown bear. No one knows, where and when he met Mishka, but for a long time they are together (excluding her current trip). However, best friends are important too. John is Chris' best friend."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Once walking with his friend, John gave Chris the following problem:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At the infinite horizontal road of width "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"w"},{"kind":"text","text":", bounded by lines "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y = w"},{"kind":"text","text":", there is a bus moving, presented as a convex polygon of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices. The bus moves continuously with a constant speed of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" in a straight "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Ox"},{"kind":"text","text":" line in direction of decreasing "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" coordinates, thus in time "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"only "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" coordinates"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of its points are changing. Formally, after time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" each of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" coordinates of its points will be decreased by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vt"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is a pedestrian in the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 0)"},{"kind":"text","text":", who can move only by a vertical pedestrian crossing, presented as a segment connecting points "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 0)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, w)"},{"kind":"text","text":" with any speed not exceeding "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus the pedestrian can move only in a straight line "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Oy"},{"kind":"text","text":" in any direction with any speed not exceeding "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and not leaving the road borders. The pedestrian can instantly change his speed, thus, for example, he can stop instantly."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please look at the sample note picture for better understanding."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We consider the pedestrian is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"hit by the bus"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if at any moment the point he is located in lies "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"strictly inside"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the bus polygon (this means that if the point lies on the polygon vertex or on its edge, the pedestrian is not hit by the bus)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given the bus position at the moment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":". Please help Chris determine minimum amount of time the pedestrian needs to cross the road and reach the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, w)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and not to be hit by the bus."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains four integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"w"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 ≤ n ≤ 10 000"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ w ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ v,  u ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of the bus polygon vertices, road width, bus speed and pedestrian speed respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines describes polygon vertices in counter-clockwise order. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them contains pair of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" - 109 ≤ xi ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ yi ≤ w"},{"kind":"text","text":") — coordinates of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th polygon point. It is guaranteed that the polygon is non-degenerate."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the single real "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the time the pedestrian needs to croos the road and not to be hit by the bus. The answer is considered correct if its relative or absolute error doesn't exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 5 1 2\n1 2\n3 1\n4 3\n3 4\n1 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5.0000000000"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Following image describes initial position in the first sample case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/2cf57a7cc68ee97e58b245c382570db74b333cf767ab88a556bab8496c6d31f0.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"703C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/703/problem/C"}